1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,385
Freelancers and small sellers lose hours to billing: invoices, payment links, and

2
00:00:05,435 --> 00:00:07,335
chasing people who haven't paid.

3
00:00:07,385 --> 00:00:09,932
AgentPay is an AI payments agent on PayPal.

4
00:00:09,982 --> 00:00:14,936
You say what you need, it does the PayPal work, and it always asks before money or

5
00:00:14,986 --> 00:00:15,790
messages move.

6
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:22,036
This is the live app, on the PayPal sandbox with Gemini as the brain.

7
00:00:22,086 --> 00:00:26,666
I ask it to bill Rohan seventy-five dollars for a website audit, due end of next

8
00:00:26,716 --> 00:00:26,955
week.

9
00:00:27,005 --> 00:00:31,397
Gemini turns that into a tool call, and the agent creates a draft with PayPal

10
00:00:31,447 --> 00:00:33,704
Invoicing, with the due date worked out.

11
00:00:33,754 --> 00:00:37,536
Sending reaches a customer, so it stops and shows an approval card.

12
00:00:37,586 --> 00:00:40,510
One click, and the invoice is sent, with a pay link.

13
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,257
Bigger requests become a plan.

14
00:00:45,307 --> 00:00:49,507
Two clients, two invoices, each drafted in PayPal with the same due date.

15
00:00:49,557 --> 00:00:52,011
Each send still gets its own approval card.

16
00:00:52,061 --> 00:00:56,320
I approve Meera's on its own, then approve the rest of the plan in one go.

17
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:07,306
For a quick sale, I ask for a twenty-dollar checkout link.

18
00:01:07,356 --> 00:01:11,607
PayPal Orders creates the order and returns a link to share with the buyer.

19
00:01:11,657 --> 00:01:14,360
A link moves no money, so it runs straight away.

20
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:18,427
Who hasn't paid me?

21
00:01:18,477 --> 00:01:22,528
The agent pulls open invoices and unpaid links, and totals what I'm owed.

22
00:01:22,578 --> 00:01:24,662
One tap drafts reminders for everyone.

23
00:01:24,712 --> 00:01:29,194
Reminders email customers, so they wait for my approval, and it tells me plainly

24
00:01:29,244 --> 00:01:31,290
which invoice PayPal couldn't remind.

25
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:41,134
Paying a collaborator works the same way.

26
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:46,028
Fifteen dollars to Alex goes through PayPal Payouts, on a US sandbox merchant app,

27
00:01:46,078 --> 00:01:47,460
only after I approve it.

28
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:56,820
Every proposal, approval and execution lands in the audit log: what the agent did,

29
00:01:56,870 --> 00:01:58,770
why it did it, and who approved it.

30
00:02:03,010 --> 00:02:08,085
AgentPay is built with FastAPI, Gemini function calling, and the PayPal Invoicing,

31
00:02:08,135 --> 00:02:09,585
Orders and Payouts APIs.

32
00:02:09,635 --> 00:02:13,796
The model only proposes; the server validates and waits for a human.

33
00:02:13,846 --> 00:02:16,520
The code and the live demo are linked below.
